# OS cruft
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
.DS_Store

# Office / PDF lock and autosave files
~$*
*.tmp

# Cloned course repos — these have their own remotes, don't vendor them here.
# See each course README for the clone command.
**/labs/*/

# Extracted archives (keep the .rar/.zip, not the unpacked copy)
**/resources/*/
# ...except small course-made folders that classmates study from directly
!semester 7/SOC4190 - Blockchain Basics and Platforms/resources/week06 - Bitcoin Transactions source/
!semester 7/SOC4190 - Blockchain Basics and Platforms/resources/week07 - games/
!semester 7/SOC4190 - Blockchain Basics and Platforms/resources/week07 - Mining source/

# Lecture videos and extracted audio — downloaded from eClass for offline
# study, never committed. Re-fetch with: python scripts/pull_vods.py
# NOTE: only the media is ignored. The .srt transcripts and .md summaries
# that sit beside them in lectures/vod/ ARE tracked — they are the study value.
*.mp4
*.m4a
*.mkv
*.webm
*.wav
*.part.mp4
*.words.json
# ...but professors' repo snapshots stay complete (a small demo video).
!**/course-repo/**/*.mp4

# ...except homework input files handed out on eClass (small, and needed to
# re-run the assignment). Generated outputs next to them stay ignored.
!**/homework/*/provided/*.mp4
!**/homework/*/provided/*.wav

# Private: my own status, not course material. The repo is public and shared
# with classmates, so these stay local only.
#   DEADLINES / STUDY-PLAN — my attendance, submissions, skipped work, plan
#   _meta/                  — eClass sync log (my submissions) + Phoenix group chat log
semester */DEADLINES.md
semester */STUDY-PLAN.md
semester */_meta/
#   PRIVATE.md              — per-folder notes on my own status, ID numbers, attempts
**/PRIVATE.md
